# G0-EOL-HASH-PORTABILITY (2026-07-31): narrow line-ending pin for the only
# artifact the experiment contract declares as LF-canonical UTF-8 text
# (hash_mode=canonical_lf_utf8_text in configs/experiment_contract.json).
# Keeping this file checked out with LF makes working-tree bytes match the
# canonical digest regardless of core.autocrlf.  The rule is limited to the
# declared asset path; it must never be extended into broad `text=auto`
# patterns and must never trigger a renormalize of tracked content.
data/development/sun_modality/source_manifest.json text eol=lf

# B0-R1-A-C3 (2026-08-03): narrow line-ending pin for the only registered
# development B0 manifest that the project audit verifies by raw SHA-256.
# The four C3 artifacts (b0_attempts.json + three evaluation JSONs) and
# their manifest.json are versioned with LF bytes; without this rule a
# Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) silently converts them to CRLF and
# the working-tree raw SHA no longer matches the manifest's declared
# SHA-256. The rule is intentionally scoped to the exact registered
# development run output directory; it must not be widened into
# `*.json text eol=lf`, `outputs/** text eol=lf`, or any `text=auto` form
# that would renormalize the whole repository.
outputs/development/s27_estg150_b0_enhanced_v10a_r1a_c3_hist56d_v1/*.json text eol=lf

